{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>On that day, etc.</b> The way of derash is well known, for the altar alludes to the slaughter of Egypt. And according to peshat it is so, and the proof is 'and he sacrificed and offered a meal offering' (Malachi 1:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The phrase 'הריגת מצרים' (slaughter of Egypt) is rendered literally; Ibn Ezra is cryptically brief about what event or figure he means."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:21.572003616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}